IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `coq-common`

-- Coroners Act 2003 (Queensland) -- part 2 (reporting deaths: ss 7, 8, 8A, 9, 10, 10AA) and part 3 division 1 as the
-- family meets it (ss 11, 11AAA, 11A, 12(1)): is the death reportable, must I report it, must a coroner investigate,
-- which coroner, and how do I challenge a decision about whether the death is reportable.
--
-- SEAT: a family member of the person who died, or another person with a sufficient interest in the death; for s 7,
-- any person who becomes aware of the death. See NOTES.md.
--
-- Every "considers", "is satisfied" and "reasonably believes" the Act gives to a coroner, the State Coroner or another
-- person is an input, never decided. Terms borrowed from other Acts (disability, NDIS participant, custody under a
-- court order, coal mine, petroleum and gas site) are asked as facts, glossed in the choices.
--
-- Unofficial version. Based on content from the Queensland Legislation website at 6 November 2026. (c) The State of
-- Queensland, CC BY 4.0. See SOURCE-LICENSE.md.
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Coroners Act 2003: reporting and investigating the death`

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `s 9 -- death in care`
-- ===================================================================================================================

-- s 9(1): "A person's death is a death in care if, when the person died--" (a) to (f). The heads use terms of other
-- Acts (Disability Services Act 2006, Forensic Disability Act 2011, Mental Health Act 2016, Public Health Act 2005,
-- Adoption Act 2009, Child Protection Act 1999, NDIS Act): the person chooses the head that fits, glossed below. s 9(3):
-- it does not matter that the person died somewhere other than where they ordinarily lived for being in care. s 9(4)
-- ("private dwelling") is folded into the glosses of heads (a)(iii), (e) and (f).
DECLARE `Care at the time of death` IS ONE OF
    `(a) a person with a disability living in a level 3 accredited residential service, a department-funded disability accommodation service, or a health-funded residential service that is not a private dwelling or aged care facility`
    `(aa) a forensic disability client being taken to or detained in the forensic disability service, or on accompanied treatment or absence, or awaiting transfer to a mental health service`
    `(b) an involuntary patient detained in or being transported to or from an authorised mental health service, on supervised limited community treatment or absence, or detained under an emergency examination authority`
    `(c) under the chief executive's guardianship under the Adoption Act 2009, section 57 or 65`
    `(d) a child in the chief executive's custody or guardianship, placed under an assessment care agreement, or under a child protection order giving custody or long-term guardianship to someone other than a parent`
    `(e) an NDIS participant not living in a private dwelling or aged care facility, receiving a relevant class of supports from a registered NDIS provider`
    `(f) not living in a private dwelling or aged care facility, receiving services under the Commonwealth's Disability Support for Older Australians Program or another prescribed Commonwealth program`
    `none of these`

GIVEN `the care` IS A `Care at the time of death`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 9 -- a death in care` `the care` IF
    CONSIDER `the care`
    WHEN `none of these` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- s 7(2) singles out heads (a), (e) and (f).
GIVEN `the care` IS A `Care at the time of death`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 7(2) -- a death in care under s 9(1)(a), (e) or (f)` `the care` IF
    CONSIDER `the care`
    WHEN `(a) a person with a disability living in a level 3 accredited residential service, a department-funded disability accommodation service, or a health-funded residential service that is not a private dwelling or aged care facility` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `(e) an NDIS participant not living in a private dwelling or aged care facility, receiving a relevant class of supports from a registered NDIS provider` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `(f) not living in a private dwelling or aged care facility, receiving services under the Commonwealth's Disability Support for Older Australians Program or another prescribed Commonwealth program` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `s 10 -- death in custody`
-- ===================================================================================================================

-- s 10(1): "A person's death is a death in custody if, when the person died, the person was-- (a) in custody; or (b)
-- escaping, or trying to escape, from custody; or (c) trying to avoid being put into custody." (2): "custody means
-- detention, whether or not by a police officer, under-- (a) an arrest; or (b) the authority of a court order; or (c)
-- the authority of an Act of the State, other than-- (i) the Education (General Provisions) Act 2006; or (ii) the Mental
-- Health Act 2016; or (iii) the Forensic Disability Act 2011; or (d) the authority of an Act of the Commonwealth."
DECLARE `Custody at the time of death` IS ONE OF
    `in custody`
    `escaping, or trying to escape, from custody`
    `trying to avoid being put into custody`
    `not in, escaping from or avoiding custody`

DECLARE `Authority for the detention` IS ONE OF
    `an arrest`
    `a court order`
    `an Act of Queensland other than the Education (General Provisions) Act 2006, the Mental Health Act 2016 or the Forensic Disability Act 2011`
    `the Education (General Provisions) Act 2006, the Mental Health Act 2016 or the Forensic Disability Act 2011 only`
    `an Act of the Commonwealth`
    `no detention`

GIVEN `the custody` IS A `Custody at the time of death`
      `the authority` IS AN `Authority for the detention`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 10 -- a death in custody` `the custody` `the authority` IF
        `the person was in or near custody`
    AND `the detention is custody`
    WHERE
        `the person was in or near custody` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the custody`
            WHEN `not in, escaping from or avoiding custody` THEN FALSE
            OTHERWISE TRUE
        `the detention is custody` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the authority`
            WHEN `the Education (General Provisions) Act 2006, the Mental Health Act 2016 or the Forensic Disability Act 2011 only` THEN FALSE
            WHEN `no detention` THEN FALSE
            OTHERWISE TRUE

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `s 10AA -- health care related death`
-- ===================================================================================================================

-- s 10AA(1): a death "after the commencement" "at any time after receiving health care that-- (a) either-- (i) caused or
-- is likely to have caused the death; or (ii) contributed to or is likely to have contributed to the death; and (b)
-- immediately before receiving the health care, an independent person would not have reasonably expected that the
-- health care would cause or contribute to the person's death." (2): the same for a failure to provide health care that
-- was sought. (3): "contributes" means the person would not have died at that time but for the care (or the failure).
-- (4): the "independent person" is appropriately qualified and has regard to all relevant matters; that judgment is an
-- input. The commencement of s 10AA is not in the deposited text; deaths are taken to be after it (fork F1).
DECLARE `Health care and the death` IS ONE OF
    `health care the person received caused, or is likely to have caused, the death`
    `health care the person received contributed, or is likely to have contributed, to the death (without it the person would not have died when they did)`
    `health care was sought but not provided, and the failure caused, or is likely to have caused, the death`
    `health care was sought but not provided, and the failure contributed, or is likely to have contributed, to the death (had it been provided the person would not have died when they did)`
    `health care played no such part`

GIVEN `the part health care played` IS A `Health care and the death`
      `an independent person would not have expected it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 10AA -- a health care related death` `the part health care played` `an independent person would not have expected it` IF
        `health care played a part`
    AND `an independent person would not have expected it`
    WHERE
        `health care played a part` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the part health care played`
            WHEN `health care played no such part` THEN FALSE
            OTHERWISE TRUE

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `s 8A -- unnatural death`
-- ===================================================================================================================

-- s 8A: "An unnatural death includes the death of a person who dies at any time after receiving an injury if-- (a) the
-- injury caused the death; or (b) both of the following apply-- (i) the injury contributed to the death; (ii) the person
-- would not have died if the person had not received the injury." An "includes" provision: when its limbs fail, whether
-- the death was otherwise violent or unnatural is asked.
DECLARE `An injury and the death` IS ONE OF
    `an injury caused the death`
    `an injury contributed to the death, and without it the person would not have died`
    `an injury contributed to the death, but the person would have died anyway`
    `no injury played a part`

GIVEN `the injury` IS AN `An injury and the death`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 8A -- an unnatural death by injury` `the injury` IF
    CONSIDER `the injury`
    WHEN `an injury caused the death` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an injury contributed to the death, and without it the person would not have died` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `s 8 -- reportable death`
-- ===================================================================================================================

-- s 8(1): "A person's death is a reportable death only if the death is a death to which subsection (2) and subsection
-- (3) both apply." (2): in Queensland, or outside it if (i) the body is in Queensland, (ii) the person ordinarily lived
-- in Queensland, (iii) was on a journey to or from somewhere in Queensland, or (iv) the death was caused by an event in
-- Queensland. (3): (a) identity unknown; (b) violent or otherwise unnatural; (c) suspicious circumstances; (d) health
-- care related; (e) no cause of death certificate issued and none likely; (f) death in care; (g) death in custody; (h)
-- in the course of or as a result of police operations. (4): "However, a death that happened outside Queensland is not
-- a reportable death if the death has been reported to a non-Queensland coroner." (5): "Despite subsections (1) to (3),"
-- a voluntary assisted dying death "is not a reportable death." "Only if", and two flat negatives: each failure is a no.
DECLARE `Where the death happened` IS ONE OF
    `in Queensland`
    `elsewhere in Australia`
    `outside Australia`

DECLARE `Is the death reportable` IS ONE OF
    `yes: the death is a reportable death (s 8)`
    `no: the death was a voluntary assisted death (s 8(5))`
    `no: the death happened outside Queensland and has been reported to a coroner there (s 8(4))`
    `no: the death has none of the connections with Queensland s 8(2) requires`
    `no: the death is none of the kinds s 8(3) lists`

DECLARE `The death` HAS
    `where it happened` IS A `Where the death happened`
    `the body is in Queensland` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person ordinarily lived in Queensland` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person was on a journey to or from Queensland` IS A BOOLEAN
    `an event in Queensland caused it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `reported to a non-Queensland coroner` IS A BOOLEAN
    `voluntary assisted dying` IS A BOOLEAN
    `identity unknown` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the injury` IS AN `An injury and the death`
    `otherwise violent or unnatural` IS A BOOLEAN
    `suspicious circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the part health care played` IS A `Health care and the death`
    `an independent person would not have expected it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `no cause of death certificate and none likely` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the care` IS A `Care at the time of death`
    `the custody` IS A `Custody at the time of death`
    `the authority` IS AN `Authority for the detention`
    `police operations` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `d` IS A `The death`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 8(3)(b) -- violent or otherwise unnatural` `d` IF
        `s 8A -- an unnatural death by injury` (`d`'s `the injury`)
    OR  `d`'s `otherwise violent or unnatural`

GIVEN `d` IS A `The death`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 8(2) -- connected with Queensland` `d` IF
        `in Queensland`
    OR  `d`'s `the body is in Queensland`
    OR  `d`'s `the person ordinarily lived in Queensland`
    OR  `d`'s `the person was on a journey to or from Queensland`
    OR  `d`'s `an event in Queensland caused it`
    WHERE
        `in Queensland` MEANS
            CONSIDER `d`'s `where it happened`
            WHEN `in Queensland` THEN TRUE
            OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `d` IS A `The death`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 8(3) -- of a listed kind` `d` IF
        `d`'s `identity unknown`
    OR  `s 8(3)(b) -- violent or otherwise unnatural` `d`
    OR  `d`'s `suspicious circumstances`
    OR  `s 10AA -- a health care related death` (`d`'s `the part health care played`) (`d`'s `an independent person would not have expected it`)
    OR  `d`'s `no cause of death certificate and none likely`
    OR  `s 9 -- a death in care` (`d`'s `the care`)
    OR  `s 10 -- a death in custody` (`d`'s `the custody`) (`d`'s `the authority`)
    OR  `d`'s `police operations`

GIVEN `d` IS A `The death`
GIVETH AN `Is the death reportable`
`s 8 -- reportable death` `d` MEANS
    IF `d`'s `voluntary assisted dying`
    THEN `no: the death was a voluntary assisted death (s 8(5))`
    ELSE IF `outside Queensland` AND `d`'s `reported to a non-Queensland coroner`
         THEN `no: the death happened outside Queensland and has been reported to a coroner there (s 8(4))`
         ELSE IF NOT (`s 8(2) -- connected with Queensland` `d`)
              THEN `no: the death has none of the connections with Queensland s 8(2) requires`
              ELSE IF NOT (`s 8(3) -- of a listed kind` `d`)
                   THEN `no: the death is none of the kinds s 8(3) lists`
                   ELSE `yes: the death is a reportable death (s 8)`
    WHERE
        `outside Queensland` MEANS
            CONSIDER `d`'s `where it happened`
            WHEN `in Queensland` THEN FALSE
            OTHERWISE TRUE

@export Is the death a "reportable death" under the Coroners Act 2003 (Qld), so that it must be reported and a coroner may investigate it?
GIVEN `where it happened` IS A `Where the death happened` @desc Where the person died
      `the body is in Queensland` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If the death happened outside Queensland: is the body in Queensland?
      `the person ordinarily lived in Queensland` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the person who died ordinarily live in Queensland at the time of death?
      `the person was on a journey to or from Queensland` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the person, when they died, on a journey to or from somewhere in Queensland?
      `an event in Queensland caused it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the death caused by an event that happened in Queensland?
      `reported to a non-Queensland coroner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If the death happened outside Queensland: has it been reported to a coroner (or the equivalent) where it happened?
      `voluntary assisted dying` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the person die after taking, or being given, a voluntary assisted dying substance under the Voluntary Assisted Dying Act 2021?
      `identity unknown` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it not known who the person who died is?
      `the injury` IS AN `An injury and the death` @desc Whether an injury (at any time before, even months before) caused or contributed to the death
      `otherwise violent or unnatural` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Apart from an injury, was the death violent or otherwise unnatural?
      `suspicious circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the death happen in suspicious circumstances?
      `the part health care played` IS A `Health care and the death` @desc What part health care, or a failure to provide health care that was sought, played in the death
      `an independent person would not have expected it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would an independent, appropriately qualified person not have reasonably expected the health care (or the failure) to cause or contribute to the death, judged when the care started or was sought?
      `no cause of death certificate and none likely` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has no doctor issued a cause of death certificate, with none likely to be issued?
      `the care` IS A `Care at the time of death` @desc Whether the person was, when they died, in one of the kinds of care the Act lists
      `the custody` IS A `Custody at the time of death` @desc Whether the person was, when they died, in custody, escaping from it, or trying to avoid it
      `the authority` IS AN `Authority for the detention` @desc The authority for that custody or detention (or the one they were avoiding)
      `police operations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the death happen in the course of, or as a result of, police operations (for example a police pursuit or an evacuation)?
GIVETH AN `Is the death reportable`
DECIDE `Is the death reportable question` IS
    `s 8 -- reportable death` (`The death` WITH
        `where it happened` IS `where it happened`
        `the body is in Queensland` IS `the body is in Queensland`
        `the person ordinarily lived in Queensland` IS `the person ordinarily lived in Queensland`
        `the person was on a journey to or from Queensland` IS `the person was on a journey to or from Queensland`
        `an event in Queensland caused it` IS `an event in Queensland caused it`
        `reported to a non-Queensland coroner` IS `reported to a non-Queensland coroner`
        `voluntary assisted dying` IS `voluntary assisted dying`
        `identity unknown` IS `identity unknown`
        `the injury` IS `the injury`
        `otherwise violent or unnatural` IS `otherwise violent or unnatural`
        `suspicious circumstances` IS `suspicious circumstances`
        `the part health care played` IS `the part health care played`
        `an independent person would not have expected it` IS `an independent person would not have expected it`
        `no cause of death certificate and none likely` IS `no cause of death certificate and none likely`
        `the care` IS `the care`
        `the custody` IS `the custody`
        `the authority` IS `the authority`
        `police operations` IS `police operations`)

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `s 7 -- the duty to report a death`
-- ===================================================================================================================

-- s 7(1): "This section applies if-- (a) a person becomes aware of a death that appears to be a reportable death; and
-- (b) the person does not reasonably believe that someone else has already reported, or is reporting, the death".
-- (2): a relevant service provider for a death in care under s 9(1)(a), (e) or (f) must report "regardless". (3): "The
-- person must immediately report the death to-- (a) if the death happened in the course of or as a result of police
-- operations--the State Coroner or a Deputy State Coroner; or (b) if the death is a death in custody--the State Coroner
-- or a Deputy State Coroner; or (c) otherwise--a police officer or coroner. Maximum penalty--25 penalty units." (7):
-- anyone may report a death they consider may be reportable. "Immediately" has no number of days, so the duty is not
-- written as a regulative rule with WITHIN (NOTES.md). "This section applies if": when it does not, the answer is no.
DECLARE `Must I report the death` IS ONE OF
    `yes: report it immediately to the State Coroner or a Deputy State Coroner (s 7(3)(a) or (b)); maximum penalty 25 penalty units`
    `yes: report it immediately to a police officer or a coroner (s 7(3)(c)); maximum penalty 25 penalty units`
    `no: s 7 does not require you to report it, as you reasonably believe someone else has reported or is reporting it; you may still report it (s 7(7))`
    `no: s 7 does not require you to report it, as you are not aware of a death that appears to be reportable; you may still report it if you consider it may be reportable (s 7(7))`

GIVEN `aware of a death that appears reportable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I reasonably believe someone else has reported it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I am the relevant service provider` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the care` IS A `Care at the time of death`
      `police operations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a death in custody` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Must I report the death`
`s 7 -- the duty to report` `aware of a death that appears reportable` `I reasonably believe someone else has reported it` `I am the relevant service provider` `the care` `police operations` `a death in custody` MEANS
    IF NOT `aware of a death that appears reportable`
    THEN `no: s 7 does not require you to report it, as you are not aware of a death that appears to be reportable; you may still report it if you consider it may be reportable (s 7(7))`
    ELSE IF `I reasonably believe someone else has reported it` AND (NOT (`I am the relevant service provider` AND `s 7(2) -- a death in care under s 9(1)(a), (e) or (f)` `the care`))
         THEN `no: s 7 does not require you to report it, as you reasonably believe someone else has reported or is reporting it; you may still report it (s 7(7))`
         ELSE IF `police operations` OR `a death in custody`
              THEN `yes: report it immediately to the State Coroner or a Deputy State Coroner (s 7(3)(a) or (b)); maximum penalty 25 penalty units`
              ELSE `yes: report it immediately to a police officer or a coroner (s 7(3)(c)); maximum penalty 25 penalty units`

@export Must I report the death, and to whom (Coroners Act 2003 (Qld) s 7)?
GIVEN `aware of a death that appears reportable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you aware of a death that appears to you to be a reportable death (violent or unnatural, suspicious, unexpected after health care, in care or custody, no cause of death certificate, identity unknown, or in police operations)?
      `I reasonably believe someone else has reported it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you reasonably believe someone else has already reported the death, or is reporting it, to the police or a coroner?
      `I am the relevant service provider` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the provider of the residential service or accommodation, or the NDIS provider, that was caring for the person who died?
      `the care` IS A `Care at the time of death` @desc Whether the person was, when they died, in one of the kinds of care the Act lists
      `police operations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the death happen in the course of, or as a result of, police operations?
      `a death in custody` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the person, when they died, in custody, escaping from custody, or trying to avoid being put into custody?
GIVETH A `Must I report the death`
DECIDE `Must I report the death question` IS
    `s 7 -- the duty to report` `aware of a death that appears reportable` `I reasonably believe someone else has reported it` `I am the relevant service provider` `the care` `police operations` `a death in custody`

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `ss 11, 12(1) -- must a coroner investigate`
-- ===================================================================================================================

-- s 11(2): "A coroner must, and may only, investigate a death if the coroner-- (a) considers the death is a reportable
-- death ...; and (b) is not aware that any other coroner is investigating the death." (3): "Also, a coroner must
-- investigate a death if the State Coroner directs" (under (4): (a) the State Coroner considers it reportable, or (b) the
-- Minister has directed it). s 12(1): "A coroner must not investigate a death, unless directed to do so by the Minister
-- or by the State Coroner under section 11(4)(b), if-- (a) the death happened in another State and has been reported to
-- a non-Queensland coroner; or (b) the death happened outside Australia."
DECLARE `Direction to investigate` IS ONE OF
    `no direction`
    `the State Coroner directed it, considering the death reportable (s 11(4)(a))`
    `the Minister directed it, or the State Coroner directed it on the Minister's direction (s 11(4)(b))`

DECLARE `Must a coroner investigate` IS ONE OF
    `yes: a coroner must investigate, because of a direction (s 11(3), s 12(1))`
    `yes: a coroner must investigate, considering the death reportable (s 11(2))`
    `no new investigation: another coroner is already investigating the death (s 11(2)(b))`
    `no: a coroner must not investigate a death outside Australia, or in another State and reported to a coroner there, without the Minister's direction (s 12(1))`
    `no: a coroner may investigate only a death the coroner considers reportable, or one directed (s 11(2), (3))`

GIVEN `where it happened` IS A `Where the death happened`
      `reported to a non-Queensland coroner` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the coroner considers it reportable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `another coroner is investigating` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the direction` IS A `Direction to investigate`
GIVETH A `Must a coroner investigate`
`ss 11, 12(1) -- a coroner must investigate` `where it happened` `reported to a non-Queensland coroner` `the coroner considers it reportable` `another coroner is investigating` `the direction` MEANS
    IF `s 12(1) bars it` AND (NOT `the Minister directed`)
    THEN `no: a coroner must not investigate a death outside Australia, or in another State and reported to a coroner there, without the Minister's direction (s 12(1))`
    ELSE IF `directed`
         THEN `yes: a coroner must investigate, because of a direction (s 11(3), s 12(1))`
         ELSE IF `the coroner considers it reportable`
              THEN IF `another coroner is investigating`
                   THEN `no new investigation: another coroner is already investigating the death (s 11(2)(b))`
                   ELSE `yes: a coroner must investigate, considering the death reportable (s 11(2))`
              ELSE `no: a coroner may investigate only a death the coroner considers reportable, or one directed (s 11(2), (3))`
    WHERE
        `s 12(1) bars it` MEANS
            CONSIDER `where it happened`
            WHEN `outside Australia` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `elsewhere in Australia` THEN `reported to a non-Queensland coroner`
            OTHERWISE FALSE
        `the Minister directed` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the direction`
            WHEN `the Minister directed it, or the State Coroner directed it on the Minister's direction (s 11(4)(b))` THEN TRUE
            OTHERWISE FALSE
        `directed` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the direction`
            WHEN `no direction` THEN FALSE
            OTHERWISE TRUE

@export Must a coroner investigate the death (Coroners Act 2003 (Qld) ss 11 and 12(1))?
GIVEN `where it happened` IS A `Where the death happened` @desc Where the person died
      `reported to a non-Queensland coroner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If the death happened elsewhere in Australia: has it been reported to a coroner in that State or Territory?
      `the coroner considers it reportable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a coroner consider the death to be a reportable death?
      `another coroner is investigating` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is another coroner already investigating the death?
      `the direction` IS A `Direction to investigate` @desc Whether the State Coroner or the Minister has directed that the death be investigated
GIVETH A `Must a coroner investigate`
DECIDE `Must a coroner investigate question` IS
    `ss 11, 12(1) -- a coroner must investigate` `where it happened` `reported to a non-Queensland coroner` `the coroner considers it reportable` `another coroner is investigating` `the direction`

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `ss 11(7), 11AAA -- which coroner investigates`
-- ===================================================================================================================

-- s 11AAA(3): "A person's death is a mining related reportable death if-- (a) the person's death is a reportable death
-- under section 8(3)(b); and (b) the person dies at any time after receiving a mining related injury that-- (i) caused
-- the death; or (ii) contributed to the death and without which the person would not have died; and (c) the person
-- receives the mining related injury-- (i) at a coal mine; or (ii) at a mine; or (iii) at or in a petroleum and gas
-- site; and (d) the person's injury is not intentionally self-inflicted." (4): a mining related injury is an injury
-- from coal mining operations, mining or quarrying operations, or data acquisition, petroleum tenure or water monitoring
-- activities (terms of other Acts, asked as one fact). (1): such a death "must be investigated by-- (a) the Mining and
-- Resources Coroner; or (b) if [that coroner] is not available ...--another coroner directed by the State Coroner."
-- s 11(7): "Despite subsection (2), only the State Coroner, a Deputy State Coroner or a coroner approved under subsection
-- (8) may investigate ... (a) a death in custody that is an unnatural death; (b) a death mentioned in section 8(3)(h),
-- other than a death in custody, that is an unnatural death." Where both could apply, s 11AAA is taken first (fork F2).
DECLARE `Where the injury was received` IS ONE OF
    `at a coal mine`
    `at a mine`
    `at or in a petroleum and gas site`
    `somewhere else`

GIVEN `reportable as violent or unnatural` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the injury` IS AN `An injury and the death`
      `an injury from mining or petroleum operations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `where received` IS A `Where the injury was received`
      `intentionally self-inflicted` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 11AAA(3) -- a mining related reportable death` `reportable as violent or unnatural` `the injury` `an injury from mining or petroleum operations` `where received` `intentionally self-inflicted` IF
        `reportable as violent or unnatural`
    AND `s 8A -- an unnatural death by injury` `the injury`
    AND `an injury from mining or petroleum operations`
    AND `at a mining place`
    AND (NOT `intentionally self-inflicted`)
    WHERE
        `at a mining place` MEANS
            CONSIDER `where received`
            WHEN `somewhere else` THEN FALSE
            OTHERWISE TRUE

DECLARE `Which coroner investigates` IS ONE OF
    `the Mining and Resources Coroner, or if that coroner is not available another coroner the State Coroner directs (s 11AAA(1))`
    `only the State Coroner, a Deputy State Coroner or a coroner approved by the Governor in Council (s 11(7))`
    `any coroner who considers the death reportable (s 11(2)), or the coroner the State Coroner directs (s 11(3))`

GIVEN `reportable as violent or unnatural` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the injury` IS AN `An injury and the death`
      `an injury from mining or petroleum operations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `where received` IS A `Where the injury was received`
      `intentionally self-inflicted` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a death in custody` IS A BOOLEAN
      `police operations` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Which coroner investigates`
`ss 11(7), 11AAA -- which coroner` `reportable as violent or unnatural` `the injury` `an injury from mining or petroleum operations` `where received` `intentionally self-inflicted` `a death in custody` `police operations` MEANS
    IF `s 11AAA(3) -- a mining related reportable death` `reportable as violent or unnatural` `the injury` `an injury from mining or petroleum operations` `where received` `intentionally self-inflicted`
    THEN `the Mining and Resources Coroner, or if that coroner is not available another coroner the State Coroner directs (s 11AAA(1))`
    ELSE IF `reportable as violent or unnatural` AND (`a death in custody` OR `police operations`)
         THEN `only the State Coroner, a Deputy State Coroner or a coroner approved by the Governor in Council (s 11(7))`
         ELSE `any coroner who considers the death reportable (s 11(2)), or the coroner the State Coroner directs (s 11(3))`

@export Which coroner must or may investigate the death: the Mining and Resources Coroner, a senior coroner, or any coroner (Coroners Act 2003 (Qld) ss 11(7), 11AAA)?
GIVEN `reportable as violent or unnatural` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the death violent or otherwise unnatural (including a death caused by an injury, or by an injury without which the person would not have died)?
      `the injury` IS AN `An injury and the death` @desc Whether an injury caused or contributed to the death
      `an injury from mining or petroleum operations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the injury from coal mining operations, mining or quarrying operations, or petroleum and gas data acquisition, tenure or water monitoring activities?
      `where received` IS A `Where the injury was received` @desc Where the person received the injury
      `intentionally self-inflicted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the injury intentionally self-inflicted?
      `a death in custody` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the person, when they died, in custody, escaping from custody, or trying to avoid being put into custody?
      `police operations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the death happen in the course of, or as a result of, police operations?
GIVETH A `Which coroner investigates`
DECIDE `Which coroner investigates question` IS
    `ss 11(7), 11AAA -- which coroner` `reportable as violent or unnatural` `the injury` `an injury from mining or petroleum operations` `where received` `intentionally self-inflicted` `a death in custody` `police operations`

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `s 11A -- challenging a decision about whether the death is reportable`
-- ===================================================================================================================

-- s 11A(1): "A person dissatisfied with a coroner's decision about whether a death that happens after the commencement
-- of this section is a reportable death may apply for an order about whether it is a reportable death." (2): to the
-- State Coroner, or, if the coroner is the State Coroner, to the District Court. (3): "A person dissatisfied with the
-- State Coroner's decision under subsection (2)(a) may apply to the District Court." (4): "An application under
-- subsection (3) must be made within 14 days after the person receives written reasons for the decision." Only the
-- subsection (3) application has a time limit (finding 4). The commencement of s 11A is not in the deposited text; the
-- death is taken to be after it (fork F1).
DECLARE `Whose decision about reportability` IS ONE OF
    `a coroner other than the State Coroner decided`
    `the State Coroner decided, as the investigating coroner`
    `the State Coroner decided my application for review of another coroner's decision`

DECLARE `Can I challenge the reportability decision` IS ONE OF
    `yes: apply to the State Coroner (s 11A(2)(a)); s 11A sets no time limit`
    `yes: apply to the District Court (s 11A(2)(b)); s 11A sets no time limit for this application`
    `yes: apply to the District Court within 14 days after you receive the State Coroner's written reasons (s 11A(3), (4)); you are within time`
    `no: an application to the District Court after the State Coroner's decision must be made within 14 days after you receive the written reasons (s 11A(4)), and that period has ended`

GIVEN `whose decision` IS A `Whose decision about reportability`
      `the day I received the written reasons` IS A DATE
      `the day I apply` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Can I challenge the reportability decision`
`s 11A -- challenging the reportability decision` `whose decision` `the day I received the written reasons` `the day I apply` MEANS
    CONSIDER `whose decision`
    WHEN `a coroner other than the State Coroner decided` THEN `yes: apply to the State Coroner (s 11A(2)(a)); s 11A sets no time limit`
    WHEN `the State Coroner decided, as the investigating coroner` THEN `yes: apply to the District Court (s 11A(2)(b)); s 11A sets no time limit for this application`
    WHEN `the State Coroner decided my application for review of another coroner's decision` THEN
        IF `the day I apply` `is on or before` (`the last day of the 14 days after` `the day I received the written reasons`)
        THEN `yes: apply to the District Court within 14 days after you receive the State Coroner's written reasons (s 11A(3), (4)); you are within time`
        ELSE `no: an application to the District Court after the State Coroner's decision must be made within 14 days after you receive the written reasons (s 11A(4)), and that period has ended`

@export I disagree with the coroner's decision about whether the death is a reportable death. To whom can I apply, and am I in time (Coroners Act 2003 (Qld) s 11A)?
GIVEN `whose decision` IS A `Whose decision about reportability` @desc Whose decision you disagree with
      `the day I received the written reasons` IS A DATE @desc The date you received the written reasons for the decision (ISO 8601); used only for an application to the District Court after the State Coroner's review
      `the day I apply` IS A DATE @desc The date you apply, or will apply (ISO 8601)
GIVETH A `Can I challenge the reportability decision`
DECIDE `Can I challenge the reportability decision question` IS
    `s 11A -- challenging the reportability decision` `whose decision` `the day I received the written reasons` `the day I apply`

@export The State Coroner refused my review about whether the death is reportable. What is the last day to apply to the District Court (Coroners Act 2003 (Qld) s 11A(4))?
GIVEN `the day I received the written reasons` IS A DATE @desc The date you received the State Coroner's written reasons (ISO 8601)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Last day to apply to the District Court about reportability question` IS
    `the last day of the 14 days after` `the day I received the written reasons`
